Windows installer: desktop shortcuts HST Writer, HST Sheets and HST Slides, chosen on the setup-type page.

The installer created one desktop shortcut, "HST Office <version>" (the Start Center), behind the
"Create a shortcut on desktop" box of the Ready to Install page. Users look for the three apps.
- scp2 folderitem_writer/calc/impress: a desktop shortcut per app (same name, target, icon and
  AppUserModelID as its Start menu entry). Each belongs to its own helper file,
  program/desktophelper_<module>.txt, in that app's brand module with ComponentCondition
  CREATEDESKTOPLINK=1: the shortcut is installed only with its app and only when the box is
  ticked, and uninstall removes it with that component. A major upgrade removes the old product's
  shortcuts first, so they are never doubled. The Start menu entries were already there.
- setup_native Package_misc.mk: the three helper files (copies of desktophelper.txt).
- Setup type page: the box "Create desktop shortcuts" ("Tạo lối tắt trên màn hình nền"), ticked by
  default (CREATEDESKTOPLINK is 1 when the package has desktop shortcuts), under the default-apps box
  and shown for Typical and Custom. It replaces the Ready to Install page's box for the same property,
  so the choice is asked once. Silent installs keep the default (1); CREATEDESKTOPLINK=0 leaves
  every desktop shortcut out, the existing "HST Office" one included.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_msi_app_desktop_shortcuts.py; windows-smoke (scripts/windows/check-app-shortcuts.ps1:
shortcuts after install, none on the desktop with CREATEDESKTOPLINK=0, none left after uninstall).
